            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P4 · Kubernetes Cluster Stopped Reporting\n**WHAT:** Kubernetes Cluster Stopped Reporting: telemetry_health signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `dev` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `kubernetes-platform` (kubernetes / kube_cluster, tier3)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Observability or configuration hygiene is degraded. No direct customer impact, but our ability to see or govern the estate is reduced.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** Absence of cluster telemetry is binary.\n**OWNER:** cloud-engineering · support best-effort · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Kubernetes Cluster Stopped Reporting` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-k8s-workload` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `kubernetes-control-plane.dev.kubernetes-platform` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-k8s-workload-availability` · no error-budget impact (non-production)\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Kubernetes Cluster Stopped Reporting — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P4.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Kubernetes Cluster Stopped Reporting — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Kubernetes Cluster Stopped Reporting\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-k8s-workload-availability`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
